e old parties are  carrying on but I think it's changed  they just want to carry on and do  business as usual the status quo when  what we need in this country is  fundamental change easy you're talking  now about the great realignment of  politics kind of ripping up the rulebook  yeah I just wonder if actually this is  more about a group of people who are  passionate remain errs who the thing  that unites them is a second referendum  getting together over brexit and  actually the most likely thing to happen  perhaps is that the party leaders decide  that actually you can be ignored because  your votes were already written in and  you're all going to lose your seats on  the next night well the dup have  exercised quite a lot of influence in  this Parliament and there are 10 DUP  already there are 11 of us and so in a  hung parliament a relatively small  number of MPs can actually make a  difference which is that I do think we  need a realignment we are trying to  break a system which is usually rigged  in favour of some of stablish parties I  think we can overcome that now there's  no doubt that we actually have to  completely tear up our electoral system  altogether and have a proper system of  proportional representation which better  reflects the modern tapestry of Britain  but right now can we make a go of this  can we make a change with  try and I definitely think we can and  you can be fighting stressing at the  next election I certainly don't intend  to leave the field look this is the  community I'm from and I grew up in and  the reason why I left the Labour Party  this week is because I believe the party  has betrayed my community we scored the  highest remain vote in the country in  2016 I stood on stood on my own personal  platform which committed to campaign and  do everything to stop the Tory heart  brexit and that is not what the party is  doing and that's why I have decided to  leave it but this is my community I  represent it I've got no intention of